the binfmt_elf.c:load_elf_binary() hunk in my previous patch was wrong.
It is fixed in this one.

I also fixed the one in binfmt_elf.c:load_elf_binary() but left
binfmt_elf.c:create_elf_tables() alone as I'm not quite sure the best
way to handle that.

Would it be best to send the fs/{binfmt_elf,compat_ioctl}.c patches to a
different list (lkml?) or maintainer?

On Wed, 2004-12-15 at 03:10 -0800, Jeremy Huddleston wrote:
> In .10-rc3-bk8, we get a bunch of these:
> warning: ignoring return value of `copy_to_user', declared with
> attribute warn_unused_result
>=20
> I've started cleaning it up, but I'm going to bed... so I thought I'd
> send it here and let someone else use it as a starting point for the
> rest of it.

--=20
Jeremy Huddleston <eradicator@gentoo.org>

